{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "T21-2e: call-site string lane. count_a's `s` is passed a string literal by one caller and an untypable local-call result by another; the closed string edge among typable callers plus subscript-only use selects the String* lane, so `s[i]` is fn_string_ascii_at and no allocating fn_index/item_at appears. first's `s` is also passed an array literal, a concrete non-string caller, so it keeps the boxed parameter and the generic subscript. The .txt golden pins that the untypable caller (make(4)) still reaches the slow body correctly on both tiers.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_count_a_#",
      "expect": [
        "call\tfn_string_ascii_at_p, fn_string_ascii_at",
        "call\tfn_len_s_p, fn_len_s"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        "call\tfn_index_p, fn_index",
        "call\titem_at_p, item_at",
        "call\tfn_len_p, fn_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "in_func": "_first_#",
      "forbid": [
        "call\tfn_string_ascii_at_p, fn_string_ascii_at"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
